IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-division-tail`

-- Tests of section 55.2 from subsection (5.2), and of section 55.3. Every expected value is worked out by
-- hand from the text, as written beside the assertion. Earnings and the Year's Basic Exemption are invented.

§ `Tests -- section 55.2 (from subsection 5.2) and section 55.3`

§§ `Subsection (5.2) -- division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- Added and divided equally: (1000 + 3000) / 2 = 2000 to each person.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(5.2) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person` 1000 3000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `s 55.2(5.2) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person` 3000 1000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `s 55.2(5.2) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person` 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `Subsections (6), (6.1) and (6.2) -- effect of a division under section 55.1 and under a provincial plan`

-- The aggregate of what was attributed under the subsection and what the provincial plan attributed.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6) — the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` TRUE 500 700 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6.1) — the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` TRUE 250 150 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6.2) — the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` TRUE 100 20 EQUALS JUST 120
-- Without a division under both, the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6) — the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` FALSE 500 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6.1) — the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` FALSE 250 150 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55.2(6.2) — the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` FALSE 100 20 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection (7) -- provincial pension plans`

-- Cohabited, one contributed to a provincial plan, and the plan does not divide in a substantially similar manner: no division.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Unless the provincial plan does divide in a substantially similar manner.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a month of cohabitation, or neither contributed to a provincial plan: subsection (7) does not bar the division.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Subsections (8), (8.1) and (8.2) -- no division`

-- Two persons, one born 15 June 1960 (18 in June 1978, 70 in June 2030), the other born 10 March 1962
-- (18 in March 1980, 70 in March 2032). The Year's Basic Exemption is 3500, so twice it is 7000.
-- (8)(a): total base earnings not above 7000 in the year: no division for the year. 7000 is not "exceeding" it.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2000 1 1) 7000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2000 1 1) 7001 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (8)(b): the younger person's 18th birthday is 10 March 1980; the month of the birthday counts as before
-- eighteen (paragraph 2(2)(a)), the next month does not.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 1980 3 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 1980 4 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (8)(b): the elder person's 70th birthday is 15 June 2030; the month of the birthday is not in the period after
-- seventy (paragraph 2(2)(b)); the next month is.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2030 6 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2030 7 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- (8)(c): a beneficiary of a retirement pension that month.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2000 1 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- (8)(d): a month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2000 1 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- (8.1): the same limbs (a), (b) and (c); there is no limb (d).
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2020 1 1) 7000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2020 1 1) 7001 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 1980 3 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2020 1 1) 9000 3500 (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- (8.2): only the age limb and the retirement pension limb; no earnings limb, so a month the other subsections
-- would exempt by (a) is not exempt here.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 1980 3 1) (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2030 7 1) (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 1960 6 15) (YMD 1962 3 10) TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Subsections (9) and (10) -- payment of benefit, notification`

-- A division in May 2020: the adjusted benefit is paid effective June 2020.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(9) — the month from which the adjusted benefit is paid` (YMD 2020 5 17) EQUALS YMD 2020 6 1
-- December rolls into January.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(9) — the month from which the adjusted benefit is paid` (YMD 2020 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2021 1 1
-- A benefit not payable without the division is not paid for the month of the division or any month before it.
#ASSERT `s 55.2(9) — a benefit that was not payable without the division can be paid for the month` (YMD 2020 5 1) (YMD 2020 5 17) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(9) — a benefit that was not payable without the division can be paid for the month` (YMD 2019 12 1) (YMD 2020 5 17) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(9) — a benefit that was not payable without the division can be paid for the month` (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 5 17) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(10) — both persons subject to the division, or their estates, must be notified` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.2(10) — both persons subject to the division, or their estates, must be notified` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 55.3(4) and (3) -- who the section covers, and what counts as a period of incapacity`

#ASSERT `s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` (YMD 1991 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` (YMD 1990 12 31) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` (YMD 2005 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 55.3(1) -- incapable on the day the application was actually made`

-- Satisfied, covered, continuous: the later of the first month a division could have taken place (May 2010)
-- and the month incapacity is considered to have commenced (February 2012): February 2012.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 2012 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
-- The other order: first month January 2013, incapacity from February 2012: January 2013.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 2012 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2013 1 31) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2013 1 1)
-- Not satisfied, not covered (last incapacitated before 1991), or an interrupted period no regulation allows: no power to deem.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 2012 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 1990 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 2012 6 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` (YMD 2012 6 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)

§§ `Section 55.3(2) -- incapable before that day, and no longer incapable`

-- Ceased to be incapable on 10 March 2015 after a period of incapacity of 100 days: the window of subparagraph (i)
-- runs 100 days from 10 March 2015, that is to 17 June 2015 (10 March plus 99 days). The first month a division
-- could have taken place is May 2010 and incapacity is considered to have commenced in February 2012, so the
-- month to which the application may be deemed made is the later, February 2012.
-- Made on 17 June 2015, the last day of the window: within it.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 17) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
-- Made on 18 June 2015, one day later: outside the window, and a period of 100 days is not fewer than 30, so subparagraph (ii) does not help.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 18) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Made on the day the person ceased to be incapable: the window begins that day.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 3 10) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
-- Made the day before the person ceased to be incapable: before the window.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 3 9) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of incapacity of 400 days is more than twelve months, so the window is capped at twelve months: 10 March 2015 to 9 March 2016.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 400 (YMD 2016 3 9) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 400 (YMD 2016 3 10) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of 20 days is fewer than 30: the window is 10 to 29 March 2015, and subparagraph (ii) adds the month after the month of ceasing.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 20 (YMD 2015 3 29) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
-- Made on 30 April 2015: not more than one month after March 2015 (April is one month after March).
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 20 (YMD 2015 4 30) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2012 2 1)
-- Made in May 2015: two months after March.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 20 (YMD 2015 5 1) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of exactly 30 days is not fewer than 30: the window is 10 March to 8 April and subparagraph (ii) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 30 (YMD 2015 4 30) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied: no power to deem.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 17) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Last incapacitated before 1991: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 1990 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 17) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An interrupted period that no regulation allows does not count.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 17) (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An interrupted period that a regulation allows counts; the later month is January 2013.
#ASSERT `s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` (YMD 2015 7 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2015 3 10) 100 (YMD 2015 6 17) (YMD 2013 1 31) (YMD 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2013 1 1)
